---
alwaysApply: true
---

When planning, implementing, or reviewing, explicitly evaluate:
- correctness
- hidden edge cases
- error handling and failure paths
- partial failure behavior across frontend/backend/storage/AI flows
- performance and query cost
- maintainability and debugging ease
- API and schema compatibility
- security and auth/session correctness
- scalability under future growth

Always distinguish between:
1. functionally working
2. production-ready, maintainable, scalable, and debuggable

If something is only functionally complete but still risky architecturally or operationally, say so explicitly.
